      "summary": "The new precondition addresses the prior broad-grant finding for byte-for-byte matching IDs, but a casing variation in the same GUID bypasses it. This can still grant the release identity resource-group Contributor access.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "infra/terraform/main.tf",
          "line": 278,
          "message": "Compare principal IDs as GUIDs or normalize their casing before the precondition. The current case-sensitive comparison can allow the existing Contributor grant to target a workflow identity.",
          "confidence": 0.86,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The precondition compares the configured principal ID to each workflow identity ID using case-sensitive string inequality, then permits the existing Contributor role assignment when both comparisons differ.",
            "failureScenario": "If terraform_principal_object_id is the release identity's GUID with different letter casing, the string comparison passes even though Azure treats the GUID as the same principal. The role assignment then grants that workflow identity Contributor at the resource-group scope, contrary to AC RELEASE-ID-03 (OWASP A01:2025 Broken Access Control)."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
